Further work can now be specific: a timestamped Hillman passage beside its Greek; a person connected by a document to instruction; the Enochic numerical and verbal correspondences; a disputed calendar adjustment and its consequences; or the same dated witnesses assessed under the Gnoli and de Jong reconstructions. “Babylon” as an institutional function is the project’s comparison; ethnic identity and inherited culpability are separate from that model. Modern political and biological claims are outside this essay’s historical account.
